                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Fentanyl is one of the leading causes of death for Americans aged 18 to 45, and this dangerous drug flowed into our country during the Biden administration. Back in 2018, President Trump signed into law the SUPPORT for Patients and Communities Act, which helps fight fentanyl overdoses by expanding access to life-saving treatments and recovery services. Today I proudly voted to reauthorize these life-saving programs.",
